Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD) on the morning of February 11 during his visit to Brunei.
University of Brunei Darussalam is the largest center of higher education and scientific research in Brunei, and ranks third in the university ranking in the region.
The University of Brunei Darussalam is one of the symbols of Vietnam-Brunei cooperation in education and training.
The University of Brunei Darussalam officially established a cooperative relationship with Vietnam FPT University in July 2013, and the main cooperation area is English training.
In addition to English, French, German, Japanese, and Korean, the University of Brunei Darussalam has also included Vietnamese in its curriculum.
During the visit to the University of Brunei Darussalam, the Prime Minister of Vietnam Nguyen Tan Dung and his wife had an exchange with students of Vietnamese language class.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is happy that more and more foreigners are learning Vietnamese, and he will actively contribute to promoting the image of Vietnamese culture and local characteristics to the world.
The Prime Minister of the Government, Pheung Amnim, expressed his belief and hope that the Vietnamese language teacher team of University of Brunei Darussalam would become stronger and stronger; the students of Vietnamese class would be more and more interested in Vietnamese language, and would strive to learn it fluently as soon as possible, and become the messenger of the friendly cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also took the opportunity to communicate with Vietnamese students studying English at FPT-UBD Global Center in Chanh Muong District, Quang Nam Province, via video, to learn about their learning situation, especially during the pandemic.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, believed that the cooperation relationship between Vietnam FPT University and Brunei University, especially the FPT-UBD Global Center, was a vivid symbol of the cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei in education.
At the same time, we hope that the students of the center will make greater progress in their studies and make positive contributions to the friendly and cooperative relations between Vietnam and the two countries.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly appreciated the achievements of the two countries in education cooperation during his discussions with the Minister of Education of Brunei and leaders of Brunei University. These achievements include the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, as well as the initiative of Brunei University to include Vietnamese language in the teaching curriculum.
Prime Minister Lim Jong-hyeon hopes that the University of Brunei Darussalam will continue to pay attention to ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and further expand the scale of Vietnamese language classes.
The Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Tan Dung, also highly evaluated the positive effects of cooperation between the two countries on the basis of the Memorandum of Understanding on Educational Cooperation signed in April 2014; he suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively carry out various short-term exchange training projects, such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Prayut Chan-o-cha highly appreciated the establishment of the first branch of the University of Brunei Darussalam in Vietnam; he believed that the university would become stronger in terms of regional and world development; and he hoped to further expand cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
Prime Minister and Mrs. Fan Mingcheng planted a commemorative tree in the campus of the University of Brunei Darussalam and left a message in the commemorative book.
Prime Minister Lim has wished that the University of Brunei Darussalam will continue to develop and contribute more power to the education industry of Brunei, and develop deeper and broader cooperation with Vietnam's educational and training institutions.
(Finish)
Vietnam News Agency
“Important Engine of Global Recovery” - chinanews.com
