I read this book in my second year of high school just to kill time. I thought I wouldn't get addicted to a book like this, since I wasn't really interested in web novels in the first place.
Then... he fell into a hole.
In terms of the plot, the whole book is quite light and pleasant. When Ye Zhu was still in the game, even though the guilds were fighting each other, it was not heavy at all because they were often killed by Ye Sheng.
As for the part of the competition, it wrote a little bit of bitterness about the change of the times (probably because I am too sentimental).
I spent a lot of time studying in high school two to read the whole book, but I just couldn't stop.
The full-time description of characters and emotional lines is amazing, and some characters only appear occasionally, but they will leave a deep impression on people. Characters such as Ye Xiu, Huang Shuang, and Su Mocha have a large number of fans, and characters such as Jiang Bo Tiao and Chu Yunxiao who are not in the center of writing are also very popular. In a light novel about e-sports, it is hard to find a character that is extremely disliked. This is the success of full-time in character description.
In terms of love lines, full-time workers don't have the problem of the thousands of beautiful women in the palace, which is the bane of web novels. All the characters in the novel have a common point, that is, they like the game Honor and most of them want a straightforward victory.
There are small conspiracies, but no big ones, and everyone seems so simple and cute.
This is perhaps also why there aren't any unlikable roles in full-time.
The full-time IP is very large, and it is also due to this.
Regardless of the cultural phenomenon of web novels, this book is a good read.
He really does give you some blood and a little bit of inspiration.
I want to become a full-time animator in April this year.
