I appreciate you, and I want you to know it!
The first factor that decides a person's job satisfaction is not the salary, but whether they are given enough attention and appreciation in their work.
According to Maslow's hierarchy of needs theory, after the basic needs of human beings are met, the most urgent need is the satisfaction of psychological needs - the hope of being understood, affirmed, and appreciated.
It is true that for Chinese people, most of them are “love you in their hearts but can’t say it out loud”, even if they have love, gratitude and praise, they will keep it in their hearts and won’t say it out loud.
The author elaborates on five languages of appreciation in the book: positive words, quality time, acts of service, sincere gifts, and physical touch.
I think it's not important to know what the five languages of appreciation are, but to be able to use them from the bottom of your heart to appreciate and be grateful to the people around you, whether they are family, friends or colleagues.
Actually, the more intimate the relationship, the more we need to appreciate and be grateful to each other, so that our lives can become more beautiful.
If you learn to appreciate, enterprises can also retain talents to a certain extent and reduce the turnover rate.
Thank you to the translator for bringing us the wonderful thoughts and the world from abroad.
Because of the differences between the languages, such as the cultural backgrounds of China and the West, if you have the chance, you can read the original version of the author and I believe you will gain more.
Thanks again to the authors, translators, and editors for their hard work!
