I am not really recommending reading it
I read this a long time ago, and I just happened to come across it and write a review.
This book is not so much a collection of short stories as it is a collection of fragments of life about love.
The writing style of this book is extremely dull, like plain water, and the phrasing is to the extreme in pursuit of simplicity. The plot is as quiet and dull as a street in the afternoon of summer.
Each short story is a fragment of time from ordinary life, with no beginning and no ending.
The songs were eventually collected together and titled "What We Talk About When We Talk About Love".
I think this collection of short stories, and its title, is a kind of performance art. The author wants to express that love is not just the joys and sorrows of life on stage, but also the urban legend of being worn out and shabby; it is not just the sticky and glue-like relationship between you and me, but also the life that is as plain as water, the monotonous and tasteless daily life, and the helplessness and escape from reality, as well as the confusion about the future.
Reading this book, you may recall the quarrelling couple around you, the boring marriage of the acquaintance, and the unpleasant relationship.
This is the reason why I do not recommend reading it. From the aesthetic point of view, the writing and plot of the book are tasteless, unless you live in a world of turbulent waves or a world of sweetness like living in a candy castle. Otherwise, you will feel that it is strange and boring to read it.
The daily events are not particularly striking or expansive in terms of thought, nor do they broaden one's mind and vision (this is different from Marquez's Love in the Time of Cholera), and the brief segments do not explore any issues, such as what kind of mistake led to the failure of love.
What are the reasons for the protagonist's broken marriage?
So I don't recommend reading this book, whether you read it or not doesn't matter much.
The author's ideas are expressed more through techniques and forms rather than story plots, which is also the reason why the reading experience of this book is not good.
